<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zinkekra</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zinkekra is an archaeological site in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fezzan">Fezzan</a> region of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>, a fortified hilltop settlement above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadi-al-ajal">Wadi al-Ajal</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garamantian-empire">Garamantian Empire</a> identify the citadel at Zinkekra as the royal centre of the Garamantes during their formative phase. The capital later moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garama">Garama</a> on the valley floor.</p></div>
